      "question": "Is a money market account 100% safe?",
      "answer": "A money market account is covered by FDIC insurance up to $250,000 per depositor, per FDIC-insured bank, for each account ownership category, and that coverage has limits. Any balance above $250,000 in one category at one bank is uninsured. The account is covered only if the bank itself is FDIC-insured, so an account at a bank without FDIC insurance has no FDIC protection. Spreading deposits across ownership categories or across more than one FDIC-insured bank keeps more of a large balance within the limits."
    },
